{
  "$comment": "Everything the wall game plays by (distances in world units, the wall's cells `cell` across; times in seconds). wall: its size (a portrait block, the same on every screen), `breakShare`: the share of its cells that brings it down (its HP is that share, so the bar and the hole are the same thing), `noise`: how much the weak lines steer a hit, `gap`: how far behind the next gate is (even, and farther than the camera's off the wall, so it's walked through). camera: upright, the wall's between the bar at the top and the cards, `clear` off both (the HUD's units; `feet` more under it, for the crew), taking at most `tall` of the screen's height; on a wide screen (from its `aspect` on) the share it takes and how far up it stands (`floorAt`); `side`: the frame seen each side of it on a narrow one; `zoom`: nearer than that (1: just so), `up`: higher, `pitchDrop`: how far it looks down (higher for it); `rollDeg`: tilted, if the effect's on. Its `fight`: how much of the way to the enemies it goes, how far up it moves besides, how soon (a second's share), how much of the wall's room they fill, how close it gets at most, how far it looks down, the room each side of them, where they stand. wallHp: by number (past the list: the last x `hpGrowth`^n). wallMaterials: wall by wall; round again (from `roundFrom`) after the last, in other colours. materials: `look` (the pattern), colours, `core`: the colour of its deepest layers, `dust`, `chip`: debris size, `hit`: its sound, `cash`: what its damage pays (1 if not given). punch: the damage, and PUNCH HARDER: the first level's given (after wall 1), and later ones at the walls in `given` (a tool each) to players who haven't bought up to that level by then, the next ones cost `costs` in turn, then x `costGrowth` each, `mult` its effect level by level (the last repeats). auto: what's given to those who don't buy: one of a kind of the crew at a wall, if there's none yet; a boost, up to wall `boostsUntil`, once there's `boostsAfter` x its bricks unspent as a wall begins and it's been there to buy for `boostsWait` walls (the player's own pick first). And money lying about spent for them as a wall begins, up to wall `buysUntil`: one PUNCH HARDER level and up to `hires` of the best of the crew, each while there's `buysAfter` x its price, if they've bought nothing for `idleWalls` walls and the last one took `slow` seconds or more (a catch-up: every wall, it races away). cash: `perDamage` and `wallBonus` (x its HP) as a wall goes. floating: what drifts across while playing, from wall `fromWall`, `first` seconds in, then `every` so long (from, to), the kinds in `turn` (cash instead of one that's not there yet), each there for `stays`: cash pays `share` of the wall's HP (cash boosts count), `least` at least; the chest, for a video, its `share`; frenzy all damage x `mult` for `seconds`. away: back after `after` seconds or more, the crew's earned `share` of what it would have, `mostWalls` x the wall's HP at most; the same again for a video (a floating one). nudge: from wall `wall` (ever reached), what can be bought left for `after` seconds, a hand points at the best of it. bricks: what a wall brings (base + perWall x its number). crew: helpers (the first of the first kind's given when its wall's reached); each copy costs x `crewGrowth` more; there from wall `wall` on (ever reached); `dps`: damage a second each; `every`: seconds between one's hits; `size`: how big; `z`: how far from the wall it stands (crewRows: all of them `away` more from it, their rows `spread` times as far apart, `width` times as wide); `style`: leap (headbutts) or throw; `shows`: how many are drawn. crewBoosts: the crew's own boosts: from `at` copies on, x `mult`, for `bricks` (+ `typeBricks` for each place down the list). boosts: the others, there from a wall or a number of copies on. weak: the weak spot (from wall `wall`): `mult` its hit, `radius` around it that counts (of the screen's height), hit again within `window` the combo goes up a step (`combo`, `comboSteps` of them to start with). shows: from which wall (ever reached) on the boosts' row, the wardrobe's button and the shop's are there. shop: what's sold where the platform has purchases (the phone app; CrazyGames once it's let in; locally with ?shop=1, mocked): `once` (had for good, restored on another device) or `consumable`; `price`: shown where the store says none; `give`: weapon `levels`, cash worth `cashWalls` of the wall's HP, `medals`, a `look` of that rarity not had yet, `noAds` (no breaks; videos stay), `cash` x, `autoHold` (a tap on HOLD keeps it on). medal: the one behind every `every`th wall from wall `wall` on, if nothing else is behind it (enemies, a boss) nor a boss's gate in sight past it; it's worth `times` its wall's number. rarity: the seven rarities, common to prismatic (looks' `rarity`; tools' grades: as it came, then each grade up, to mythic), each's colour, card frame (ItemFrame02_Single_<frame>) and stars (`premium`: the rainbow ones). relics: bought with medals (cashed in), each level costs `cost` x `growth`^level (up to `max`): `times` x`each` a level, `plus` +`each`, `less` x`each` (shorter), `start`: a rewind starts at wall 1 + `each` a level; a medal spent stops giving its damage. ranks: the crew's own, for good (through rewinds too), bought with gems (bosses drop them: boss `gems`, one more every `gemsEvery` walls): each kind's next rank costs `cost` (x `growth` for each place down the crew's list), and its damage is x `mult`; each rank a hat on all of that kind (`hats`: hard hat, viking hat, crown; tools/build-hats.mjs). hold: a finger held down on the wall punches where it is from the start; the HOLD button is there from the first rewind on, and `perSecond` (slower than AUTO and than tapping), from `after` seconds held; the HOLD button's held, the way between walls goes `rush` times as fast (`on`: false, and there's no holding). powers: the power-ups set off down the right side: there from wall `wall`, on for `seconds`, charged again in `charge`; auto hits `perSecond` times a second. rooms: the colour of the gates, the floor and the dark (`room`) and of the gates' lights (`accent`, `boss` at a boss's), the next in the list every `every` walls. enemies: what waits behind some walls (`on`: false, and there's nothing: the game as it was without them; ?enemies=0 or 1 tries it, and so does the debug panel). boss: behind every `every`th wall from wall `from`, which is of `material`; `hp`: a share of the wall's, `seconds` to beat it in; beaten, `cash` (x the wall's HP) and `bricks` more; kinds in turn (with each rewind, from the next), each boss bigger than the one before (`grow`, and `growRun` for each rewind, at most `most`) and, every `colorEvery` bosses and with each rewind, in the next of `colors`: `paint` bone only the bones, `hue` all of it turned to that hue (from its own, `base`; at least this vivid, `sat`). `pair`: two of them, half the health each (`x` along the gate, `next` colours on). minions: behind every `every`th wall, from wall `from` (not a boss's); `count` of them (one more every `more` walls, at most `most`), `hp` each (a share of the wall's), `cash` for one (x its HP); kinds in turn. circles: on the minions in the first `fights` fights ever won: a hit within `radius` (of the screen's height) of one does x `mult`. farm: the minions that come while a boss that got away isn't called back. rewind: from wall `wall` (reached; its popup opens by itself, once ever, from wall `popup`, or when a boss gets away before that): back to wall 1 without cash, bricks or crew, PUNCH HARDER kept at `keep` of its level (no more gifts of it, nor of the crew's next kinds), boosts kept, all damage + `perMedal` for each medal, for good. tools: (a tool kept over levels is made better: its edges glow in the next of `grades` each time, green, blue, purple) the first from PUNCH HARDER level `from` on, kept for as many levels as `levels` says (the first, the second ...), and after those `levelsAfter` each (so each goes up the grades: green, blue, purple, gold, red): the first type in its first two colours, then the types in turn, in the next colour (tiers, for the metal; `glow`: it shines) every `perTier` levels; `own`: its own colours instead, one each time it comes round (`band`: its cuffs'); `bite`: how a hit spreads (wide: across the face, deep: into it).",
